# 🎮 Game UI Transformation — From Website to Immersive Game Interface

Transform the current Skribbl.io clone from a "website that happens to be a game" into a **full-fledged game interface** inspired by Minecraft, arcade games, and retro gaming aesthetics — enhanced with 21st.dev-style effects (particles, glowing elements, animated backgrounds, micro-interactions).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Theme Direction**: The plan proposes a hybrid aesthetic — **Minecraft-inspired pixel art** meets **neon arcade glow** (think Minecraft meets Tron). This keeps the existing neon color palette but adds blocky pixel textures, 8-bit fonts, and game HUD elements. If you'd prefer a pure Minecraft dirt/stone look instead, let me know.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No New Dependencies**: All effects will be built with vanilla CSS + existing React. No Tailwind, no Framer Motion, no external component libraries to install. We're recreating 21st.dev-quality effects from scratch — particle systems, glow effects, animated borders — all in pure CSS and canvas.

## Open Questions

- **Sound Effects**: Would you like me to also add game sound effects (click sounds, correct guess chime, countdown tick, etc.)?
- **Mobile Support**: Should the game UI be optimized for mobile/touch or is desktop-first fine?

