## Proposed Changes

The transformation is organized into **6 phases**, each targeting a specific area of the UI. Every phase makes the app feel less like a website and more like you're *inside a game*.

---

### Phase 1: Design System Overhaul — Game Typography, Colors & Textures

The foundation. Replace web-standard fonts and clean gradients with a game-native feel.

#### [MODIFY] [index.css](file:///c:/Users/91986/OneDrive/Pictures/web3task/frontend/src/index.css)

**Typography:**
- Replace `Space Grotesk` body font with **`"Press Start 2P"`** (Google Fonts) — the iconic pixel font used in retro/Minecraft-style games
- Keep `Outfit` for large headings but add `text-shadow` glow effects
- All labels, scores, and HUD text use pixel font

**Color Palette Update:**
- Keep the neon purple/cyan core but add game-specific colors:
  - `--xp-gold: #ffd700` — for XP/score displays
  - `--health-red: #ff3333` — for timer warnings
  - `--mana-blue: #4488ff` — for drawing mode indicators
  - `--rare-green: #55ff55` — for correct guesses (Minecraft rare item green)
- Add CSS custom properties for pixel border patterns

**Background:**
- Replace the subtle grid with an **animated starfield/pixel grid** pattern
- Add scanline overlay effect (subtle CRT-like horizontal lines) for retro game feel
- Dark vignette at screen edges (like game viewport)

**New CSS Classes:**
- `.pixel-border` — Minecraft-style 3px stepped borders with inner highlight and outer shadow
- `.game-panel` — Replaces `.glass` with a darker, more opaque panel with pixel border frame
- `.neon-glow` — Reusable neon text-shadow/box-shadow glow effect
- `.xp-bar` — Animated fill bar (used for timer, score progress)
- `.tooltip-game` — Game-style tooltip with arrow and pixel border

